{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/775900-houses-in-devil-s-due","id":775900,"title":"Houses in Devil's Due","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-28T04:00:10-08:00","id":775900,"title":"Houses in Devil's Due","content":"Hey folks, wondering your thoughts on this. I'm preparing a Devil's Due adventure for Dark Ages, and as a bit of character background the players are going to choose Demon Houses.<br /> <br /> Now, while the Houses don't matter mechanically in Devil's Due, we were chatting about them in relation to the selection of Sins. Seven Sins, Seven Houses, so maybe if one chose a Sin that would indicate House?<br /> <br /> (again, this has no real bearing on things, but has raised a few questions that I thought it would be interesting to discus). Here are my thoughts:<br /> <br /> <b>Devils </b>\u2013 Namaru - First House \u2013 Pride<br /> Pretty Obvious<br /> <br /> <b>Scourges </b>\u2013 Asharu \u2013 Second House \u2013 Sloth<br /> They were cursed to watch humans grow old and decay, which kind of fits Sloth.<br /> <br /> <b>Malefactors </b>\u2013 Annunaki - Third House \u2013 Greed<br /> They make riches and offered such to humankind.<br /> <br /> <b>Fiends </b>\u2013 Neberu - Fourth House \u2013 Envy<br /> They see the future, and were cursed that because of them humankind would always reach for the future while ignoring the past and present.<br /> <br /> <b>Defilers </b>\u2013 Lammasu - Fifth House \u2013 Lust<br /> Pretty Obvious<br /> <br /> <b>Devourers </b>\u2013 Rabisu - Sixth House \u2013 Gluttony / Wrath<br /> Gluttony given that their curse was related to feeding (albeit animals feeding on humans), though they were also violent warriors so Wrath perhaps fits better.<br /> <br /> <b>Slayers </b>\u2013 Halaku - Seventh House \u2013 Sloth?<br /> They don\u2019t really enjoy killing, so I\u2019m not going to say Wrath.<br /> <br /> But, that gives two for Sloth, and no obvious candidate for Gluttony (with the Devourers being a reach).<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5922-volesus","name":"Volesus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T06:05:07-08:00","id":775933,"title":"","content":"In my opinion Wrath doesn't imply joy with being violent, just that you're angry and seek release in violence to calm yourself down, and the Slayers do give release in death so in that sense I could see a symbolic value to giving them Wrath while the Devourers get Gluttony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:02:04-08:00","id":776188,"title":"","content":"I see what you're saying, Karavolos. Thanks for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5922-volesus","name":"Volesus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T16:20:56-08:00","id":776258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/775900-houses-in-devil-s-due?p=775933#post775933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion Wrath doesn't imply joy with being violent, just that you're angry and seek release in violence to calm yourself down, and the Slayers do give release in death so in that sense I could see a symbolic value to giving them Wrath while the Devourers get Gluttony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded.<br /> <br /> And just to add, in the broad, while I understand why D:tF was structured the way it was (to make Demon characters another comparable &quot;splat&quot;), I always felt it just didn't quite work right, imo. I *so* liked the albeit-looser system set up in DD -- it mad tailoring a Demon character much better, as well as made a better mechanical system for various powers a Demon might have as well as give a better system-cum-thematic for Pacts and such having an influence over total power a Demon can express (it also made Faith mean something more than what it does in D:tF). <br /> <br /> Loved me some Devil's Due....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T00:21:50-08:00","id":776470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I *so* liked the albeit-looser system set up in DD -- it mad tailoring a Demon character much better </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why we want to do Devil's Due! The Pacts system contributing to over-all power really seems right, and yes, the loser system does seem to work a bit better than Demon: The Fallen! I personally can't wait to try it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5922-volesus","name":"Volesus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}